DataFrames make it easy to create new columns and rename existing ones. That's why I prefer doing data analysis with DataFrames rather than SQL tables. Say we have a dataframe shown below and we wanted to categorize the budget values into two groups: "Too high" and "Just right"

::: {#d9c02d76 .cell execution_count=1}

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (5, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Department</th><th>Budget</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Hospitality&quot;</td><td>50000</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Legal&quot;</td><td>120000</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Finance&quot;</td><td>80000</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Advertising&quot;</td><td>60000</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Sales&quot;</td><td>90000</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


